<h1><span lang="EN-US">From N Constrained Points</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-US">This command is accessible from</span> <b><i><span class="Path">Transformations &gt; From N Constrained Point</span><span lang="EN-US">s</span></i>.</b></p>
<p class="Description"><span lang="EN-US">The command</span> <b><i style="font-weight:normal; font-style:normal;"><span class="Command">From N Constrained Points</span></i></b> <span lang="EN-US">is used in 2 main cases:</span></p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered"><span lang="EN-US">To set transformation by more than 3 correspondences</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered"><span lang="EN-US">To set transformation when no exact entity match is present and needed to set correspondences by some of the co-ordinates only.</span></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The T</span><span lang="EN-US" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>ransformation</u></span> <span lang="EN-US">mode is displayed in a separated tab and the user can switch between all tabs, can make some changes or create new entities meanwhile. Each transformation matrix can be lately changed, applied to selection or activated for scanning.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The Transformation tab contains 3 main sections:</span></p>
<table class="NormalTable" style="border-spacing:0px;" cellspacing="0">
<tr class="whs4">
<td rowspan="3" valign="top" width="221.4pt" class="whs5">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/Npoints.gif" width="231px" height="677px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" width="221.4pt" class="whs8">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">1. <a href="#Template_section">Template section</a>  allows to save, modify and delete transformation templates</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr class="whs9">
<td valign="top" width="221.4pt" class="whs10">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">2. <a href="#Setup_Transformation_Section">Setup Transformation section</a>  used to define a transformation name, to set the number and the weight of each correspondence.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr class="whs4">
<td valign="top" width="221.4pt" class="whs10">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">3. <a href="#Edit_correspondence_section">Edit correspondence section</a> - used to set entity types for the correspondences</span></p>
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">4. <a href="#Define_Entity_Sub_section">Define Entity sub-section</a>  used to set values for the chosen entity by different methods.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>See also</b></span><span lang="EN-US">: Tutorials for creating constrained transformation.</span></p>
<h2><span lang="EN-US"><a name="Template_section"></a>Template section</span></h2>
<p><span lang="EN-US">In the KUBE software the transformations can be easily created and modified using templates. There are no predefined templates in this mode. If the user needs to create a template it is necessary to setup a transformation and then to save it with a new name.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">Each template can be loaded from the list in later sessions of KUBE.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">In a template are saved all parameters of the correspondences and their values. Modifications in each existing template can be updated by using the button Save.</span></p>
<h2><span lang="EN-US"><a name="Setup_Transformation_Section"></a>Setup Transformation section</span></h2>
<p><span lang="EN-US">In this section should be set the number of correspondences, their weight and the meaningful coordinates. Description:</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Correspondences</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Table with all correspondences included in the calculations for the current transformation. For each correspondence the user can set:</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="88.038%" class="whs11">
<col>
<col class="whs12">
<tr valign="top" class="whs13">
<td class="whs14">
<p class="whs6"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">No</span></b></p>
</td>
<td width="641px" class="whs15">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">Number of correspondence. If it is coloured in red, then the correspondence is still not defined. If it is coloured in black  correspondence OK.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs13">
<td class="whs16">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>XYZ</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">checkboxes</span></p>
</td>
<td width="641px" class="whs17">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">For setting which ones of the coordinates will be used.</span></p>
<p class="Warning"><span lang="EN-US">The XYZ checkboxes affect the co-ordinates of the target model entities only. The target model should be very well orientated, so that the choice of constrained co-ordinates to be correct.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs13">
<td class="whs16">
<p class="whs6"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Weight</span></b></p>
</td>
<td width="641px" class="whs17">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">Choose a number in the range 1 to 10 to define the importance of the correspondence in the calculations. The bigger value means bigger influence of this correspondence over the final result.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs13">
<td class="whs16">
<p class="whs6"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">RMS</span></b></p>
</td>
<td width="641px" class="whs17">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">Information field for each correspondence. It is updated every time when a parameter of the correspondence is changed. The overall RMS is displayed right below the table. It also will change when updating parameters.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Add new button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US"> adds a new correspondence to the transformation.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Delete</span></b> <span lang="EN-US"> deletes the currently marked row in the correspondence table.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Name</b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">You have 3 choices for setting the transformation name: leave the default one, type a new name or choose an existing one from the list. <i style="font-style:normal;">The default name is Transformation N, where N is the number of the subsequent newly created transformation. When a transformation</i> <span lang="EN-US"><i style="font-style:normal;">is created the number N in the name will automatically increase.</i></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">When all correspondences are set and their primitives defined (for details see the descriptions below), press the</span> <span class="Button">Create</span> <span lang="EN-US">button. If the transformation is successfully created a message will appear asking you whether to activate the transformation for scanning or not. In case of answering Yes, have in mind that all further scanning will pass through the transformation matrix and the co-ordinates of the captured points will not be in global space.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">If you want to exit the transformation mode, then press the</span> <span class="Button">Close</span> <span lang="EN-US">button.</span></p>
<h2 class="whs18"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;"><a name="Edit_correspondence_section"></a>Edit correspondence section</span></b></h2>
<p class="whs19"><span lang="EN-US">In this section are defined the datum entities chosen for the currently marked correspondence in the table above.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US">Source Entity</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Movable datums (if the transformation is applied on these datums, their positions should be identical/closer to the correspondent target entities). Generally the source entities belong to the movable object or can be captured for future scanning. In the mode source entities can be point, circle and sphere.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US">Target Entities</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Fixed datums. Usually, the target entities are extracted from a CAD model or a reference mesh. In the mode target entities can be point, circle and sphere.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Schematic</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP166558847" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/image007.gif" width="528px" height="277px" border="0" class="img_whs20" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-US">For each correspondence should be chosen one pair of primitives. Click on the arrow button next to the datum button to select the appropriate primitive from the list. In the constrained transformation mode 3 entity types only are available:</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/Choose_datum_constrained.gif" width="138px" height="115px" border="0" class="img_whs21" alt=""></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The fourth option in this list allows the user to pick an entity from the viewport. If this option is enabled, then the user can simultaneously select entity type and define entity values. It is used for quick correspondence definition by picking predefined datums from the viewport. By default this option is disabled and each primitive must be defined by any of the available methods. Detailed description of the process follows in the <i>Define Entity sub-section.</i></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">On the left of each datum button there is a small icon showing the definition method used to set values for this datum. The meaning of each icon is explained in the table below:</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="628" class="whs22">
<col class="whs23">
<col class="whs24">
<tr valign="top" class="whs13">
<td width="7.813%" class="whs25">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/sel2.gif" width="23px" height="19px" border="0" class="img_whs26" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td width="92.188%" class="whs27">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">The values for this datum are manually input or picked as points directly from the viewport.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs13">
<td width="7.813%" class="whs28">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/sel2_red.gif" width="23px" height="20px" border="0" class="img_whs29" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td width="92.188%" class="whs30">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">The values for this datum are not yet defined.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs13">
<td width="7.813%" class="whs28">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/sel1.gif" width="23px" height="22px" border="0" class="img_whs31" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td width="92.188%" class="whs30">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">The datum is chosen from a list or picked as primitive from the viewport</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs13">
<td width="7.813%" class="whs28">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/sel3.gif" width="21px" height="20px" border="0" class="img_whs32" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td width="92.188%" class="whs30">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">The values are set by fitting datum to a custom selection</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs13">
<td width="7.813%" class="whs33">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/sel4.gif" width="20px" height="20px" border="0" class="img_whs34" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td width="92.188%" class="whs30">
<p class="whs6"><span lang="EN-US">The values will be defined lately during capture procedure.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="parameterdescription" id="P2">&#160;</p>
<p class="Note" id="P2"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">If there are not defined values, the correspondence remains undefined and transformation can not be created.</span></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<h3><span lang="EN-US"><a name="Define_Entity_Sub_section"></a>Define Entity sub-section</span></h3>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The definition dialog shown in this sub-section depends on the chosen target or source entity. Each datum definition can be set by 4 main methods:</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Capture</b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Delayed operation. It will start when all correspondences are set and Create transformation is initiated. The datums will be captured by order of their correspondences. The capturing functionality is the same as in the arm menu.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Fit to</span></b> <b>selection</b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Interactive method for setting values. The user makes a selection, press the button Fit selection and the datum parameters will be instantly filled in the edit boxes. If necessary these values can be manually changed.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Choose from list or pick entity</b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Both options refer to the same functionality  selection of an existing primitive. The user can either choose a datum from the list or directly pick it on the viewport. The datum parameters will be instantly filled in the edit boxes. If necessary these values can be manually changed.</p>
<p id="P3" class="Note"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> If you want to use <span class="Command">Pick points</span> method for datum definition and at the same time you have an active selection mode, you should first exit the selection mode by using the key <span class="Button">Esc</span> and KUBE will pass automatically to the <span class="Mode">Pick points</span> mode</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Manual co-ordinates input or pick points</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Both options refer to the same functionality  simple co-ordinate input. The user can either type manually the datum parameters in the edit boxes or pick a minimal number of points on the viewport to define the datum. The minimal number of picked points depends on the entity type.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Particularities</b></span>: For each entity definition a method is automatically selected using the following rule:</p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Pick from viewport method is enabled by default only the first time you open the transformation mode.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">If the user changes the definition method for an entity, his last choice will be set as active by default when switching to another entity definition (no matter source or target).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-US">When an entity is defined it appears as temporary datum in the viewport. Dialog description for each entity type:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_point.htm" id="a2">Point</a></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_sphere.htm" id="a3">Sphere</a></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_circle.htm" id="a4">Circle</a></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
